

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                            GIOVANNA D'ARCO







          Alberto Clerici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the advent of the spring season, Giovanna d'Arco set out to quench 
her thirst for glory.  She was tutored in the art of Marches by Hakim.  
Giovanna d'Arco studied and practiced her Marches and her skill in Marches 
went up.

  A great fleet of mighty ships carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Sea province of the Killer 
Frog Sea, ruled by Giovanna d'Arco.  The Killer Frog Sea was overrun by 
Riose (#52)'s fleet.  Riose leads approximately 3 Bowmen, 2 Fleet and 1 
Mermen.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Giovanna d'Arco cast a Bless 
spell.  Pearlgate was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected 
no armies in Pearlgate.
  Hakim cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for 
Giovanna d'Arco.

  A fleet coming from the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded the Vodka Sea, hoping to subjugate that province owned by 
Giovanna d'Arco and made up of great Seas.  Riose (#52) was in command of 
the attacking fleet.  The defending forces were commanded by the provincial 
garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown 
here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Vodka Sea (1605):

  279th   
  Bowmen  
