  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 303rd Mermen and the 285th Bowmen in reserve.  
Standing tall with his ships was Riose.  No generals were present to lead 
the forces of Giovanna d'Arco.
  Riose's fortunes took a turn for the better when his scouts located and 
occupied a prominent rock outcropping, which proved useful as an observation 
post.  Also, his wise naval maneuvers assured his forces a clear advantage.

  Across the whole front, the Veteran 280th Fleet Marines faced the 251st 
Fleet Marines, who sang out their thunderous battle hymns, inspired with a 
fanatical elan by their exalted King.  The 286th Fleet Marines flanked the 
enemy and attacked with full strength.  The 303rd Mermen swam undersea and 
attacked.  The 280th Fleet Marines fought the 251st Fleet Marines and 
smashed them like rotten oranges.
  Riose's great armada overpowered the fleet of Giovanna d'Arco and cleared 
the seas of their squadrons, dispersing their enemies.  The 280th Fleet 
Marines annihilated the 251st Fleet Marines.
  Riose's well-planned campaign effected the conquest of the Vodka Sea.  The 
acting commander withdrew to Moussoro, beaten but not discouraged.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Giovanna d'Arco cast a 
Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for Giovanna d'Arco.
  Hakim cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for 
Giovanna d'Arco.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  Giovanna d'Arco moved into Jaguardo 
(#1701) with her high-spirited army.  East of here is Chandrapur (#1801), a 
Plain area owned by no one, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors fight 
in the style of Legion.  To the north is a forbidding mass of glaciers which 
seemingly has no end.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to Giovanna d'Arco invaded the 
province of Jaguardo, a Desert area owned by Bairn (#41).  Giovanna d'Arco 
commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces were led by Bairn.  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Jaguardo (1701):

