  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 215th Camel Corps, the 243rd Light Cavalry, the 
331st Bowmen and the 332nd Bowmen in reserve.  Giovanna d'Arco marched with 
her loyal troops, jaws set in grim resolution.  Bairn led his armies 
courageously into the fray.
  The army of Giovanna d'Arco used magic to aid their cause.  Magical 
phantasmal armies fought with hers soldiers.  Giovanna d'Arco was not at all 
fortunate this day, because the sun shone directly against her men's eyes, 
giving Bairn's men a small edge.  On the other hand her wise tactical 
planning gave her forces a clear advantage.
  The Elves led by Giovanna d'Arco were not impressed by her lack of 
leadership ability.
  Across the entire front, the Elite 259th Legion were visited by a great 
Thunderbird who descended from the heavens to aid their righteous Divine 
cause, and were inspired to fanaticism by its thunderous spectacle.  They 
faced the 181st Camel Corps.  The 242nd Light Cavalry outflanked the 
undermanned enemy lines and attacked with full strength.  The horses of the 
242nd Light Cavalry were spooked by the howls of the Beasts they beheld.  
The 185th Light Cavalry outflanked the undermanned enemy lines and charged 
in with full strength.  The horses of the 185th Light Cavalry were spooked 
by the nasty smell of the Beasts they were faced with.  The 259th Legion 
battled with the 181st Camel Corps and cut them down like beanstalks.
  Giovanna d'Arco's armies shattered the army opposing them with a final 
determined charge.  The 259th Legion scattered the 181st Camel Corps in all 
directions.
  Jaguardo was overrun by the forces of Giovanna d'Arco.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Giovanna d'Arco marched her 
command into Tigerhome (#1702).


  An army coming from the empire of Giovanna d'Arco entered Tigerhome, 
hoping to subjugate that province ruled by the provincial Troll chieftain 
and made up of extensive Forests.  Giovanna d'Arco was in command of the 
attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial Troll 
chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Tigerhome (1702):

