  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 215th Camel Corps in reserve.  Giovanna d'Arco led 
her armies into the battle.  No generals were present to lead the forces of 
the provincial Troll chieftain.
  The army of Giovanna d'Arco used magic to aid their cause.  Magical 
phantasmal armies fought with hers soldiers.  Giovanna d'Arco was unlucky 
this time, for many of her skirmishers got lost in a swamp.  The provincial 
Troll chieftain thus gained a significant edge.  But Giovanna d'Arco 
deployed her forces against the provincial Troll chieftain with excellent 
tactical foresight and obtained an important tactical advantage.
  The Elves commanded by Giovanna d'Arco were disgusted with her lack of 
leadership ability.
  On the left wing, the Crack 242nd Light Cavalry were arrayed against the 
183rd Trolls.  The 185th Light Cavalry outflanked the undermanned enemy 
lines and attacked with full force.  In this sector, the 183rd Trolls 
feigned retreat, hoping to lure the enemy into more favorable ground.  But 
the trick backfired when some of the soldiers panicked, and the 183rd Trolls 
milled about in disorder.  The 242nd Light Cavalry fought with the 183rd 
Trolls and drove them back.
  Out on the right flank, the Elite 259th Legion were aided by a mighty 
Thunderbird who flew down from the stars to aid their righteous Heavenly 
cause, and were elevated to fanaticism by its thunderous splendor.  They 
faced the 182nd Trolls.  The 331st Bowmen flanked the undermanned enemy and 
charged in with full force.  The 259th Legion battled with the 182nd Trolls 
and viciously crushed them.
  The forces of Giovanna d'Arco broke through the lines of their enemy and 
were victorious.  The 242nd Light Cavalry destroyed the 183rd Trolls.  The 
259th Legion annihilated the 182nd Trolls.
  Giovanna d'Arco's host ended the campaign successfully and conquered the 
province of Tigerhome.  After the battle was over, the trolls reformed into 
a disgruntled band of mercenaries.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna d'Arco for this year.


  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna d'Arco 
treated with her ally Kwoth (#3).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally 
Hokuto (#4).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Prometeo (#5).  
Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Kahn (#6).  Giovanna d'Arco treated 
with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Agesilao 
(#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Loviatar (#92) hiked into Maicuru.  She had grown tired with Tesawa and 
was attracted there by rumors of its fine scotch.
  The captain of the 182nd Trolls felt a thirst for adventure awakening in 
his breast, and speaking eloquently of Pearlgate, persuaded his men to march 
with him to Pearlgate.
  The 183rd Trolls lost hope of finding employment in Tigerhome, so they 
mustered their strength and moved on to Marigold.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna d'Arco's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 63 gold in revenue.  13 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 177th Legion trained well and improved in quality.  40 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna d'Arco was left with 27 gold 
in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring, and I prepared to carry out my 
urgent orders.  I marched on Maicuru (#1804) with my forces.
  In early summer, I marched my forces into Cascadia (#1704).
  With the coming of the late summer season, I levied the 177th Legion in 
Cascadia to serve me.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  I failed in my attempt to cast a Tornado 
spell.
  In early winter, I attempted a Bless spell, but botched it.
  While speaking to some friendly farmers, I heard a rumor about a Loch in 
the Plesiosaurus Sea (#1406), inhabited by the Elasmosaurus.  Some say that 
the Elasmosaurus owns the Rod of Resurrection.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Watson, Squire to Hakim
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Hakim set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He practiced his Marches for many weeks, but could make no 
progress.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Hakim cast a Phantasmal Armies 
spell and illusory armies were formed for Giovanna d'Arco.
  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer arrived.  Hakim cast a 
Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for Giovanna d'Arco.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  Hakim navigated Sageleaf thoroughly, 
leaving no island uncharted, and our exploration level there has risen to 44%.
While adventuring, Hakim encountered no marauding monster.
  During early winter, Hakim cruised freely about Sageleaf, exploring its 
mysteries, and raising our exploration level in Sageleaf to 66%.  Hakim 
discovered also that Sageleaf has been the site of hard-fought battles.  
Brave and intrepid warriors have perished on its fields: the 176th Legion 
(Veteran Humans).  His efforts raised his skill in Exploring.  He 
encountered no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Hakim


From: Tiffany
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I attempted a Bless spell, but botched it.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Isis was resurrected by the 
spell cast by me.
  In late summer, I sailed into Pearlgate.
  With the coming of the fall season, I announced a plea for recruits in 
Pearlgate and was able to form the 230th Legion, the 239th Legion, the 244th 
Light Cavalry and the 248th Light Cavalry to fight for me.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Tiffany's Bless spell 
backfired and I was left with my face covered with psycho-kinetic goo.

  Thy humble servant,   Tiffany


From: Moosu, Squire to Drake
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Drake travelled to Kajaani.  While adventuring, he encountered 
no monsters.
  With the coming of the early summer season Drake searched throughout 
Kajaani for some sign of Isis.  Drake could not see Isis because Isis was 
dead.  Instead, Drake tried hard to improve his Necromancy, but he practiced 
in vain.
  With the advent of the late summer season Drake could not cast 
Resurrection on Isis because Isis was still alive.  So, Drake worked on his 
Druidism but was frustrated in his self-improvement efforts.
  With the advent of the fall season Drake cast a Bless spell.  Maplehaven 
was magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 169th 
Heavy Cavalry were Blessed and permanently destroyed.  His experience 
improved his prowess in White Magic.
  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in White Magic.  At levels 5 
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped at 3 Action, 2
Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" spells are also 
capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine who attacks 
first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  With the advent of the early winter season Drake cast a Bless spell.  
Cascadia was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies 
in Cascadia.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Drake


From: Watson, Squire to Isis
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  Isis's attempted 
cast of the Clairvoyance spell didn't work.  A strange magical counterspell 
seemed to have worked against her spell.
  During fall, Isis cruised over to Sageleaf.  She encountered no monster.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Isis moved into Tigerhome.  
During her travels this season, she was confronted by a Giant Praying Mantis.
Isis ran shamelessly and fled from the combat.


  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Isis


